A final STEP 0 audit of the corrected family reveals a deeper issue: the 7.3-million figure came from needlessly materializing the full distance-two CSP before factor recovery. A theorem-aware algorithm can recover the two edge-size factors directly in near-linear incidence time—the same work as the supposed “compact” route. I’m measuring that true mechanical cost now; if it is comparable, H fails even on Track B and the honest outcome is rejection, not a quota-blocked ship.
